

The delay-slot reorganization pass uses note-skipping neighboring-insn
lookups in three places where a DEBUG_INSN is not an executable boundary.
As a result, debug information can change skip optimization, label reuse,
and register-copy recognition.

Use the nondebug lookup helpers and add focused SPARC -fcompare-debug
tests for all three paths.

Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex 5.6 Sol, co-reviewed by Claude and Yongqiang Tian.

	PR rtl-optimization/127725

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* reorg.cc (optimize_skip): Use next_nonnote_nondebug_insn.
	(get_label_before): Use prev_nonnote_nondebug_insn.
	(fill_slots_from_thread): Use next_nonnote_nondebug_insn.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/sparc/reorg-fill-slots-regcopy-debug.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/sparc/reorg-get-label-before-debug.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/sparc/reorg-optimize-skip-debug.c: New test.

Signed-off-by: Yongqiang Tian <yqtian668@gmail.com>
